---
import { type GameEntry } from '~/lib/games';

interface Props {
  game: GameEntry;
}
const { game } = Astro.props;
const officialUrl = game.data.officialUrl ?? 'https://mana.gs/drink-the-ocean';
---

<div class="ocean-page -mx-4 -my-8">
  <section class="ocean-hero">
    <div class="ocean-shell ocean-hero-grid">
      <div class="ocean-hero-copy">
        <nav class="ocean-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/games/">Games</a><span>/</span><span>Drink the Ocean</span>
        </nav>
        <p class="ocean-kicker">BROWSER GAME / MANA VERSION</p>
        <h1>Drink the<br />Ocean</h1>
        <p class="ocean-deck">One small straw. A whole ocean to empty.</p>
        <p class="ocean-intro">
          Sip away the sea, explore the seabed it leaves behind, sell discovered treasure,
          and buy better straws. Play on your own or bring up to three friends.
        </p>
        <ul class="ocean-facts" aria-label="Game details">
          <li>Desktop browser</li><li>1–4 players</li><li>No download</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="ocean-actions">
          <a class="ocean-primary" href={officialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Play on Mana <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="ocean-secondary" href="#start">How to Play ↓</a>
        </div>
        <p class="ocean-disclaimer">Opens the official Mana game in a new tab. 1in8b is an independent player guide.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ocean-cover">
        <img src={game.data.cover} width="1200" height="675" alt="Official Mana Drink the Ocean image: a character draws water into a whirlpool using a striped straw near a wooden ship" fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption>Official game image © Mana · <a href={officialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source</a></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="ocean-shell">
    <nav class="ocean-nav" aria-label="On this page">
      <span>ON THIS PAGE</span>
      <a href="#start">Get Started</a>
      <a href="#loop">Game Loop</a>
      <a href="#bladder">Bladder &amp; Flush</a>
      <a href="#upgrades">Upgrades &amp; Tools</a>
      <a href="#regions">Areas</a>
      <a href="#coop">Solo &amp; Co-op</a>
      <a href="#tips">Tips</a>
      <a href="#controls">Controls</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <section id="start" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading">
      <p>FIRST FIVE MINUTES</p>
      <h2>How to Start Drinking the Ocean</h2>
      <span>Start with the official Mana version, then let the changing shoreline guide you.</span>
    </header>
    <div class="ocean-steps">
      <article><b>01</b><h3>Open the game</h3><p>Go to Mana and select <strong>Play Now</strong>. Let the desktop browser game finish loading.</p></article>
      <article><b>02</b><h3>Choose your session</h3><p>Start a solo game, or choose the multiplayer option to play together.</p></article>
      <article><b>03</b><h3>Drink, then empty</h3><p>Drink to lower the waterline. When your bladder fills, find an outhouse to empty it and continue.</p></article>
      <article><b>04</b><h3>Turn finds into upgrades</h3><p>Search the newly exposed seabed, sell treasure to the merchant, and get a stronger straw.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="loop" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading">
      <p>THE GAME LOOP</p>
      <h2>Drink. Discover. Upgrade. Repeat.</h2>
      <span>The reward is not just a larger straw: the island itself keeps changing.</span>
    </header>
    <div class="ocean-loop">
      <article>
        <div class="ocean-symbol">01<span>WATERLINE ↓</span></div>
        <h3>Drink the sea</h3><p>Begin with a tiny straw and gradually lower the water around the island.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="ocean-symbol">02<span>SEABED ↗</span></div>
        <h3>Explore what appears</h3><p>Walk across dried seabed, check newly revealed paths, and collect hidden valuables.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="ocean-symbol">03<span>STRAW ↑</span></div>
        <h3>Sell &amp; upgrade</h3><p>Exchange your finds with the merchant for stronger straws, then drain further.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="ocean-callout"><strong>Two real limits:</strong> drinking fills your bladder and treasure fills your bag. Return to an outhouse to empty and to the merchant to sell; these trips become more noticeable as the shoreline retreats.</p>
  </section>


  <section id="bladder" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading"><p>CAPACITY &amp; RETURN TRIPS</p><h2>Bladder, Outhouses &amp; Flush</h2><span>Why draining the sea is not just a matter of holding down a button.</span></header>
    <div class="ocean-pair">
      <article><p class="ocean-small">WHAT STOPS YOU</p><h3>When your bladder is full</h3><p>Drinking increases the bladder gauge. Once it fills, go to an outhouse and empty it to keep drinking. <strong>Iron Bladder</strong> increases capacity; it reduces how often you need to stop.</p><span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=125s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jayify gameplay · 02:05 ↗</a></span></article>
      <article><p class="ocean-small">WHAT SHORTENS THE BREAK</p><h3>Quick Flush and movement</h3><p><strong>Quick Flush</strong> cuts the time spent emptying, while movement speed reduces the run back to the outhouse and merchant. Recorded players often combine emptying, selling and shopping in one return.</p><span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rF9KFy4497U&t=830s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dr_Horse co-op · 13:50 ↗</a></span></article>
    </div>
    <p class="ocean-callout"><strong>Trade-off, not a fixed best choice:</strong> a bigger bladder gives longer continuous drinking sessions; a faster flush shortens each stop. We have not benchmarked which saves more time at each stage.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="upgrades" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading"><p>ITEMS SEEN IN ACTUAL PLAY</p><h2>Straws, Upgrades &amp; Tools</h2><span>Shop functions verified from Mana-version gameplay, with timestamps to check them.</span></header>
    <div class="ocean-shop-intro">
      <article><strong>Drink faster</strong><p>Improve suction power, straw diameter and range, or save for new straw tiers. Super, Mega and Giga straws appear during the recorded runs.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Spend less time returning</strong><p>Capacity, flush, movement and bag upgrades help reduce interruptions. Later tools can automate some draining or collect treasure.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="ocean-table-wrap"><table class="ocean-upgrade-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Observed role</th><th>Video</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Iron Bladder</th><td>Increase drinking capacity.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=1066s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">17:46 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Quick Flush</th><td>Reduce time spent emptying.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJr6WUDKPiA&t=279s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">04:39 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Treasure Magnet</th><td>Collect nearby treasure automatically.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=1066s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">17:46 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Bigger Bag / Movement Speed</th><td>Carry more valuables; travel faster to shop and outhouse.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJr6WUDKPiA&t=1848s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">30:48 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Sea Pump</th><td>Automatically drains water from the shore while active.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=2048s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">34:08 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Sponge Bomb</th><td>One-off large drain. The recorded build prompts <strong>F</strong> to throw it.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJr6WUDKPiA&t=4071s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">1:07:51 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Head Lamp</th><td>Lights up deep areas; shown in the shop.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=2438s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">40:38 ↗</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Auto Sell Charm</th><td>Automatic-selling tool listed in the shop; exact usage unverified.</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJr6WUDKPiA&t=3876s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">1:04:36 ↗</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p class="ocean-fine">Video evidence supports these tools and broad effects. No verified optimal purchase order, complete price table or universal unlock thresholds are claimed.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="regions" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading"><p>AREA PROGRESSION</p><h2>Starting Island → Lost Lagoon → Midnight Sea</h2><span>Recorded players progress through three distinct regions, not one endless beach.</span></header>
    <div class="ocean-regions">
      <article><div class="ocean-region-num">01 · START</div><h3>Starting Island</h3><p>Drain shallows to uncover reefs, treasure and the wrecked ship. When the first gate appears, decide whether to collect remaining items before entering.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=1425s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">First gate, 23:45 ↗</a></article>
      <article><div class="ocean-region-num">02 · NEXT</div><h3>Lost Lagoon</h3><p>A new shoreline and sunken temple reveal fresh treasure. The game can warn that a gate is one-way; treat that warning seriously rather than assuming you can go back.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJr6WUDKPiA&t=3754s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lagoon, 1:02:34 ↗</a></article>
      <article><div class="ocean-region-num">03 · FINAL SEA</div><h3>Midnight Sea</h3><p>The final sea contains deeper seabed discoveries, a lighthouse and giant bones. The 100% ending can arrive even when upgrades remain unpurchased.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=2268s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Final sea, 37:48 ↗</a></article>
    </div>
    <p class="ocean-callout"><strong>How to reach the next area:</strong> lower the current region's sea level until its gate becomes available, then enter when ready. Exact fixed water-depth thresholds have not been reliably established across builds.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="coop" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading">
      <p>PLAY YOUR WAY</p>
      <h2>Solo or With Friends?</h2>
      <span>Mana lists co-op support for one to four players.</span>
    </header>
    <div class="ocean-pair">
      <article>
        <p class="ocean-small">ONE PLAYER</p><h3>Take the island at your own pace.</h3>
        <p>Explore each newly exposed stretch of land, gather treasure, and decide when to return to the merchant.</p>
        <span>START WITH: NEW GAME</span>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="ocean-small">UP TO FOUR PLAYERS</p><h3>Bring friends to drain it together.</h3>
        <p>Choose MULTIPLAYER and follow the room prompts. In Dr_Horse's co-op playthrough, the players discuss using a room name and number. Their treasure sales benefit both players, but upgrades are purchased separately.</p>
        <span>START WITH: MULTIPLAYER · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rF9KFy4497U&t=330s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Co-op video ↗</a></span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="tips" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading">
      <p>PRACTICAL TIPS</p>
      <h2>What Players Actually Found Useful</h2>
      <span>Three takeaways drawn from full recorded playthroughs, not generic incremental-game advice.</span>
    </header>
    <div class="ocean-tips">
      <article><div class="ocean-tip-number">01</div><div><h3>Collect treasure as you drain.</h3><p>Newly exposed valuables finance upgrades. Jayify notes that collecting throughout a run avoids leaving a large backlog of loot far from the shop.</p><p class="ocean-evidence"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=1543s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the run · 25:43 ↗</a></p></div></article>
      <article><div class="ocean-tip-number">02</div><div><h3>Choose between immediate power and saving.</h3><p>Players debate suction upgrades versus holding funds for the next straw. Compare the shop's actual item descriptions rather than following an untested universal tier list.</p><p class="ocean-evidence"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=749s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the decision · 12:29 ↗</a></p></div></article>
      <article><div class="ocean-tip-number">03</div><div><h3>Don't confuse 100% with max upgrades.</h3><p>Two completed runs note that some equipment remains unpurchased at the end. Test the tools you care about before committing to the last transition.</p><p class="ocean-evidence"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o&t=3100s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the ending ↗</a></p></div></article>
    </div>
    <p class="ocean-fine">These observations come from recorded playthroughs, not a measured speedrun or verified optimal upgrade order.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="controls" class="ocean-shell ocean-section">
    <header class="ocean-heading">
      <p>DEVICE &amp; INPUT</p>
      <h2>Controls and Browser Support</h2>
      <span>What Mana confirms, without borrowing keybindings from the similarly named Playgama game.</span>
    </header>
    <div class="ocean-control">
      <div>
        <p class="ocean-small">OFFICIALLY LISTED INPUT</p>
        <h3>Keyboard + Mouse</h3>
        <p>Drink the Ocean on Mana is designed for a desktop browser. Use the in-game control prompts for the current key mapping; Mana's listing does not publish a complete hotkey chart. The recorded Mana version prompts F for the Sponge Bomb tool.</p>
        <a href="https://mana.gs/support" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mana browser troubleshooting ↗</a>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <strong>Mobile?</strong>
        <p>Mana currently recommends playing its games on a computer. Do not use touch-control instructions written for other Drink the Ocean versions.</p>
        <strong>Game slow to load?</strong>
        <p>Try a current desktop browser and enable graphics acceleration. Mana's support page covers common browser issues.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="ocean-shell ocean-section ocean-faq">
    <header class="ocean-heading">
      <p>QUESTIONS &amp; ANSWERS</p>
      <h2>Drink the Ocean FAQ</h2>
      <span>Six practical search-intent questions plus four questions inspired by actual playthroughs. Exact search volumes are not verified.</span>
    </header>
    <p class="ocean-faq-subhead">QUICK ANSWERS · 6</p>
    <div class="ocean-faq-list">
      {game.data.faq?.slice(0, 6).map((item) => (
        <details><summary>{item.question}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{item.answer}</p></details>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="ocean-faq-subhead ocean-faq-next">FROM REAL PLAYTHROUGHS · 4</p>
    <div class="ocean-faq-list">
      {game.data.faq?.slice(6).map((item) => (
        <details><summary>{item.question}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{item.answer}</p></details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="ocean-shell ocean-source">
    <p class="ocean-small">PLAYING A DIFFERENT VERSION?</p>
    <p>If you see a salt press or Sky Duck, you are looking at a different <em>Drink the Ocean</em> distributed through Playgama. This guide covers <a href={officialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Mana version</a>, with a merchant, treasure and co-op straws.</p>
    <p><strong>Sources checked November 16, 2026:</strong> <a href={officialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mana official listing</a> and <a href="https://mana.gs/support" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">support</a>; gameplay by <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rF9KFy4497U" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dr_Horse</a>, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7Ux72Vcb4o" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jayify</a>, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJr6WUDKPiA" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Malakye G</a> and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hnPkjIgrpPI" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Juste une run</a>. Gameplay observations come from publicly recorded videos and auto-generated transcripts; exact upgrade efficiencies and unlock thresholds have not been independently benchmarked.</p>
  </aside>
</div>

<style>
  .ocean-page{--o-ink:hsl(var(--foreground));--o-muted:hsl(var(--muted-foreground));--o-line:hsl(var(--border));--o-card:hsl(var(--card));--o-soft:hsl(var(--muted));--o-accent:hsl(var(--brand-text));background:hsl(var(--background));color:var(--o-ink);font:16px/1.6 Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;padding-bottom:5rem}
  .ocean-page *{box-sizing:border-box}
  .ocean-shell{width:min(1240px,calc(100% - 48px));margin-inline:auto}
  .ocean-hero{border-bottom:1px solid var(--o-line)}
  .ocean-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.88fr 1.12fr;gap:42px;align-items:center;min-height:520px;padding-block:42px 48px}
  .ocean-crumbs{display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:30px;color:var(--o-muted);font-size:12px}
  .ocean-crumbs a{color:inherit}
  .ocean-kicker,.ocean-heading>p,.ocean-small{color:var(--o-accent);font-size:10px;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:.16em;margin:0 0 10px}
  .ocean-hero h1{font-family:Arial Black,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:clamp(49px,6.2vw,87px);line-height:.93;letter-spacing:-.073em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0}
  .ocean-deck{font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,28px);line-height:1.2;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:17px 0 15px}
  .ocean-intro{max-width:510px;color:var(--o-muted);line-height:1.8}
  .ocean-facts{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 19px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:26px 0;font-size:13px;font-weight:750}
  .ocean-facts li:before{content:'✓';color:var(--o-accent);margin-right:8px}
  .ocean-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:25px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .ocean-primary{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;padding:12px 22px;background:var(--o-accent);color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:850;border-radius:2px}
  .ocean-primary:hover{filter:brightness(.88)}
  .ocean-secondary{font-size:13px;font-weight:800;color:var(--o-ink)}
  .ocean-disclaimer{font-size:11px;color:var(--o-muted);margin-top:16px}
  .ocean-cover{margin:0;position:relative;border:1px solid var(--o-line);background:var(--o-soft)}
  .ocean-cover img{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:3/2;object-fit:cover;display:block}
  .ocean-cover figcaption{position:absolute;left:15px;bottom:15px;padding:5px 9px;background:#123944dc;color:#fff;font-size:10px}.ocean-cover figcaption a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline}
  .ocean-nav{display:flex;overflow-x:auto;white-space:nowrap;background:var(--o-card);border:1px solid var(--o-line);border-top:0}
  .ocean-nav>*{flex:0 0 auto;border-right:1px solid var(--o-line);padding:15px 21px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--o-ink);font-size:12px}
  .ocean-nav span{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:850;color:var(--o-accent)}
  .ocean-section{padding-top:74px;scroll-margin-top:40px}
  .ocean-heading{margin-bottom:26px}
  .ocean-heading h2{font-family:Arial Black,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:clamp(28px,3.1vw,43px);line-height:1.13;letter-spacing:-.053em;margin:0 0 8px}
  .ocean-heading>span{color:var(--o-muted);font-size:14px}
  .ocean-steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:15px}
  .ocean-steps article,.ocean-loop article,.ocean-pair article,.ocean-tips article,.ocean-control>div,.ocean-control aside,.ocean-faq-list details{background:var(--o-card);border:1px solid var(--o-line);border-radius:2px}
  .ocean-steps article{padding:22px;min-height:205px}
  .ocean-steps b{font-family:Arial Black,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:35px;letter-spacing:-.06em;color:var(--o-accent)}
  .ocean-steps h3,.ocean-loop h3,.ocean-tips h3,.ocean-control h3{font-size:18px;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:12px 0 8px}
  .ocean-steps p,.ocean-loop p,.ocean-tips p,.ocean-control p,.ocean-pair p{color:var(--o-muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}
  .ocean-loop{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}
  .ocean-loop article{padding:24px}
  .ocean-symbol{height:118px;background:var(--o-soft);border-bottom:3px solid var(--o-accent);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px;color:var(--o-accent);font:850 54px/1 Arial Black,Arial,sans-serif}
  .ocean-symbol span{font:800 10px/1.4 Inter,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.11em;max-width:70px;text-align:right}
  .ocean-callout{padding:15px 20px;border:1px solid var(--o-line);background:var(--o-soft);font-size:13px;margin-top:18px;color:var(--o-muted)}
  .ocean-callout strong{color:var(--o-ink)}
  .ocean-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:18px}
  .ocean-pair article{padding:30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:250px}
  .ocean-pair h3{font-size:26px;line-height:1.24;letter-spacing:-.045em;font-weight:850;margin:0 0 14px;max-width:400px}
  .ocean-pair article>span{display:block;margin-top:auto;padding-top:24px;color:var(--o-accent);font-size:11px;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:.12em}
  .ocean-tips{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}
  .ocean-tips article{padding:24px}
  .ocean-tip-number{font:850 36px/1 Arial Black,Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--o-accent)}
  .ocean-fine{font-size:11px;margin-top:15px;color:var(--o-muted)}
  .ocean-control{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr;gap:18px}
  .ocean-control>div,.ocean-control aside{padding:30px}
  .ocean-control h3{font-size:29px;margin:12px 0}
  .ocean-control a{display:inline-block;color:var(--o-accent);font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-top:20px}
  .ocean-control aside{background:var(--o-soft)}
  .ocean-control aside strong{font-size:14px;display:block;margin-bottom:6px}
  .ocean-control aside p{margin-bottom:20px}
  .ocean-faq-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start;gap:10px}
  .ocean-faq-list details{padding:17px 20px}
  .ocean-faq-list summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;font-weight:800;font-size:14px}
